#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133516 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133726 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1d7509fa-a254-5b78-b307-3e0c4ef4d9ec" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a CDF Given a PDF With a Lower Bound"}] :question/id #uuid "38b4473a-f956-5af5-863b-387dc10b4924" :question/math-academy-id "e-13362" :question/problem "Given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n![](images/17/1714eb4797f7b318f5e957db7ab0f322fffb2eb2c9bf03f68e3acc08ec399849.svg)\n\nfind the cumulative distribution function $F(x).$" :question/worked-solution "Since our random variable $X$ has a probability distribution function $f(x)$ that is strictly positive only for $x \\geq 0,$ the cumulative distribution function takes the following form:\n\n![](images/4f/4f0d336b322f68550c50d65380e26ffb33bdd55beab0c7d429e7b4055f973b57.svg)\n\nFor the given probability density function, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{0}^{x}{e}^{-t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ \\text{ } & =-{e}^{-t}{|}_{0}^{x} \\\\  & =-{e}^{-x}+1 \\\\  & =1-{e}^{-x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the cumulative distribution function is given by\n\n![](images/9e/9e1b63a37177781672b70c3a6c01b1b752164b976b6e9982e07d510d468353aa.svg)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133517 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133727 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7b0ce833-e045-5aff-94a4-f9ad56cdb904" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a CDF Given a PDF That’s Nonzero Over All Real Numbers"}] :question/id #uuid "98dd834c-ac74-5cdd-88ee-060fd9ac689d" :question/math-academy-id "e-13363" :question/problem "Given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x) = e^{-|2x|}, \\quad x \\in (-\\infty, \\infty),\n$$\n\nfind the cumulative distribution function $F(x).$" :question/worked-solution "Since our random variable $X$ has a probability distribution function $f(x)$ that involves an absolute value, the cumulative distribution function takes the following form:\n\n![](images/40/40ebced9e322ef969e40733356aacdb3971e14276bc6ad54691aeea21b14c488.svg)\n\nLet's compute the integrals.\n\n- If $x \\leq 0,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{x}{e}^{2t}\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\frac{{e}^{2t}}{2}|}_{-\\infty }^{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{2x}}{2},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}{e}^{2t}\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\frac{{e}^{2x}}{2}|}_{x=0} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- If $x > 0,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{x}{e}^{-2t}\\,\\text{d}t & =-{\\frac{{e}^{-2t}}{2}|}_{0}^{x} \\\\  & =-\\frac{{e}^{-2x}}{2}+\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}{e}^{2t}\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{0}^{x}{e}^{-2t}\\,\\text{d}t & =\\frac{1}{2}+(-\\frac{{e}^{-2x}}{2}+\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =1-\\frac{{e}^{-2x}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the cumulative distribution function is given by\n\n![](images/92/9293ff0dab0e6c12fd143ec5f8a9d72edfce74fcddae2397f19d0e82a8b767cc.svg)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133518 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133728 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "eedcfa3d-b02b-5f96-99f4-cd0a452d272a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a CDF Given a PDF With Lower and Upper Bounds"}] :question/id #uuid "4159a407-ea9f-5728-b219-bf1afab732a2" :question/math-academy-id "e-13364" :question/problem "Given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n![](images/9d/9d755ff833ca8a9134d8f2548b6e7e26221a4814cda8a28093a345a2d321920e.svg)\n\nfind the cumulative distribution function $F(x).$" :question/worked-solution "Since our random variable $X$ has a probability distribution function $f(x)$ that is strictly positive only for $0 \\leq x \\leq 12,$ the cumulative distribution function takes the following form:\n\n![](images/fd/fd6306e35f5c55b4de635fe7d8967e7783f11c96cee2ea8adfdd17348f97a095.svg)\n\nFor the given probability density function, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{0}^{x}\\frac{1}{72}t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ \\text{ } & ={\\frac{1}{144}{t}^{2}|}_{0}^{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{144}{x}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the cumulative distribution function is given by\n\n![](images/b1/b168cb9b6e4619e7b25cddea9ee671e665d057923b9562ff50d99ce874ea8b90.svg)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133519 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133729 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3cbc399b-90f3-5acd-ac70-7345a8436978" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Probability Over an Interval Using a CDF"}] :question/id #uuid "707e3b49-9c13-50d8-8a7f-c4d5ec44e0ff" :question/math-academy-id "e-13365" :question/problem "Given that the random variable $X$ has the cumulative distribution function\n![](images/97/9792a5033ccd5f6f8198e3465899c752ddd4ae0986b324c13575c1a92e1ff3c7.svg)\n\nfind $P(2\\leq X \\leq 6).$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that for continuous random variables, it doesn't matter whether or not we include the endpoints of the interval. So we can perform this computation as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(2\\le X\\le 6) & =P(2<X\\le 6) \\\\  & =P(X\\le 6)-P(X\\le 2) \\\\  & =F(6)-F(2) \\\\  & =\\frac{{6}^{2}-25}{75}-0 \\\\  & =\\frac{11}{75}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186419957 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133729 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3cbc399b-90f3-5acd-ac70-7345a8436978" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Probability Over an Interval Using a CDF"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2e1f547c-1869-547c-823e-9966458b8f4a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419867} {:answer/id #uuid "8d811409-dae2-5c13-9164-8ada023a305c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419894} {:answer/id #uuid "ad797bab-2e14-55d8-85ab-5c933d18a216" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419905} {:answer/id #uuid "b0aaacdf-cb18-5d4c-8295-8a9b43dede71" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419907} {:answer/id #uuid "ee6abc14-8e45-5ccc-b78f-b12ee121bb95" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419926}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ad797bab-2e14-55d8-85ab-5c933d18a216" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419905} :answer-field/id #uuid "270571a9-0f7f-511a-a143-fe6af5a15b80" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419929}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "de421a60-85ed-5a5a-9a98-5df02c4cb3f4" :question/math-academy-id "q-126176" :question/problem "Given that the random variable $X$ has the cumulative distribution function\n\n$$\nF(x)={\\begin{aligned}0, & x<4 \\\\ 1-\\frac{16}{{x}^{2}}, & x\\ge 4,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfind $P(X>6).$" :question/worked-solution "The cumulative distribution function of a continuous random variable $X$ is the function $F(x)$ defined by\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x).\n$$\n\nHence, the required probability is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X>6) & =1-P(X\\le 6) \\\\  & =1-F(6) \\\\  & =1-(1-\\frac{16}{{6}^{2}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186419944 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133729 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3cbc399b-90f3-5acd-ac70-7345a8436978" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Probability Over an Interval Using a CDF"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "04fc2411-0461-5350-a6d4-77130a96a596" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419856} {:answer/id #uuid "0f9b63be-e003-513c-960b-dc0a6866add4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419860} {:answer/id #uuid "22307ec9-ce6b-54ac-8d2e-3cf6990bb045" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{36}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419866} {:answer/id #uuid "35abf0ef-ee66-53cd-a97d-5575de5686bc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{225}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419868} {:answer/id #uuid "6d30549b-41ec-5746-94b1-bdf0fddb2247" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{15}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419882}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "04fc2411-0461-5350-a6d4-77130a96a596" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419856} :answer-field/id #uuid "0f3a27a8-4efa-5646-b1d9-f25fb627f5fa" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419928}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3191d215-7e03-5aae-a424-72356e84e8e6" :question/math-academy-id "q-126177" :question/problem "Given that the random variable $X$ has the cumulative distribution function\n\n$$\nF(x)={\\begin{aligned}0, & x<0 \\\\ 1-\\frac{225}{(x+15)^{2}}, & x\\ge 0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfind $P(X\\le 5).$" :question/worked-solution "The cumulative distribution function of a continuous random variable $X$ is the function $F(x)$ defined by\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x).\n$$\n\nHence, the required probability is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le 5) & =F(5) \\\\  & =1-\\frac{225}{(5+15)^{2}} \\\\  & =1-\\frac{9}{16} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{16}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186419956 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133727 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7b0ce833-e045-5aff-94a4-f9ad56cdb904" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a CDF Given a PDF That’s Nonzero Over All Real Numbers"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0b1e4645-ce48-5f06-a7d7-34323e0d0b93" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "F(x)=\\frac{1}{(1+{e}^{2x})^{4}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419858} {:answer/id #uuid "0e41de6f-5095-5ac0-a495-3d30c7145756" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "F(x)=1-\\frac{1}{(1+{e}^{2x})^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419859} {:answer/id #uuid "794e5508-c708-5544-83e6-85e9c8ebed21" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "F(x)=\\frac{1}{(1+{e}^{2x})^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419887} {:answer/id #uuid "83be2e46-de7d-50e1-912e-11e66409165a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "F(x)=\\frac{\\pi }{2}-\\frac{1}{(1+{e}^{2x})^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419890} {:answer/id #uuid "e57de798-83cd-5d70-b368-ec17bdf4fd1b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "F(x)=1+\\frac{1}{(1+{e}^{2x})^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419923}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0e41de6f-5095-5ac0-a495-3d30c7145756" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "F(x)=1-\\frac{1}{(1+{e}^{2x})^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419859} :answer-field/id #uuid "05df3ca1-c837-5b2a-a2ca-c614521b137f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419927}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "dbdaccde-7824-5d29-93f1-f05b495a99f8" :question/math-academy-id "q-126213" :question/problem "Given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{4{e}^{2x}}{(1+{e}^{2x})^{3}},\\,x\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),\n$$\n\nfind the cumulative distribution function $F(x).$" :question/worked-solution "The cumulative distribution function of a continuous random variable $X$ is the function $F(x)$ defined by\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x)={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nFor the given probability density function, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(x) & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{x}\\frac{4{e}^{2t}}{(1+{e}^{2t})^{3}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={-\\frac{1}{(1+{e}^{2t})^{2}}|}_{-\\infty }^{x} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{(1+{e}^{2x})^{2}}+1 \\\\  & =1-\\frac{1}{(1+{e}^{2x})^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134150 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133728 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "eedcfa3d-b02b-5f96-99f4-cd0a452d272a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a CDF Given a PDF With Lower and Upper Bounds"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "65bf060c-f63e-58ca-b70b-edc87d24113f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^{2}-4}{21}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419881}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "65bf060c-f63e-58ca-b70b-edc87d24113f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^{2}-4}{21}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419881} :answer-field/id #uuid "8695f467-02b5-5934-9aba-7e6cf9cbc235" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131036}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b6a0e95b-94bf-5003-b9b0-2bdf03b33051" :question/math-academy-id "q-185532" :question/problem "Given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{21}x,\\, & 2\\le x\\le 5 \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nits cumulative distribution function is\n\n$$\nF(x)={\\begin{aligned}0,\\, & x<2 \\\\ h(x),\\, & 2\\le x\\le 5 \\\\ 1,\\, & x>5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $h(x)=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "Since our random variable $X$ has a probability distribution function $f(x)$ that is strictly positive only for $2\\le x\\le 5,$ the cumulative distribution function takes the following form:\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x)={\\begin{aligned}0, & x<2 \\\\ {\\int }_{2}^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t, & 2\\le x\\le 5 \\\\ 1, & x>5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the given probability density function, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{2}^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{2}^{x}\\frac{2}{21}t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ \\text{ } & ={\\frac{1}{21}{t}^{2}|}_{2}^{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{21}{x}^{2}-\\frac{4}{21} \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}-4}{21}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the cumulative distribution function is given by\n\n$$\nF(x)={\\begin{aligned}0,\\, & x<2, \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}-4}{21},\\, & 2\\le x\\le 5, \\\\ 1,\\, & x>5.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134158 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133726 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1d7509fa-a254-5b78-b307-3e0c4ef4d9ec" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a CDF Given a PDF With a Lower Bound"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "38c41f81-53df-5e58-be19-db1d50a00fde" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-e^{-6x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419870}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "38c41f81-53df-5e58-be19-db1d50a00fde" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-e^{-6x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419870} :answer-field/id #uuid "1a878c16-55d3-55d7-a28d-76c0dd451c37" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131062}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "445cea8c-2aa7-58ac-ac1e-76b49bacb6c1" :question/math-academy-id "q-210758" :question/problem "Given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}6{e}^{-6x},\\, & x\\ge 0 \\\\ 0,\\, & x<0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nits cumulative distribution function is\n\n$$\nF(x)={\\begin{aligned}0,\\, & x<0 \\\\ h(x),\\, & x\\ge 0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $h(x)=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "Since our random variable $X$ has a probability distribution function $f(x)$ that is strictly positive only for $x\\ge 0,$ the cumulative distribution function takes the following form:\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x)={\\begin{aligned}0, & x<0 \\\\ {\\int }_{0}^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t, & x\\ge 0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the given probability density function, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{0}^{x}6{e}^{-6t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ \\text{ } & =-{e}^{-6t}{|}_{0}^{x} \\\\  & =-{e}^{-6x}+1 \\\\  & =1-{e}^{-6x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the cumulative distribution function is given by\n\n$$\nF(x)={\\begin{aligned}0, & x<0, \\\\ 1-{e}^{-6x}, & x\\ge 0.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186419958 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133727 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7b0ce833-e045-5aff-94a4-f9ad56cdb904" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a CDF Given a PDF That’s Nonzero Over All Real Numbers"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cc767f0c-f65c-5d40-bf26-8221c3e5652f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-\\frac{e^{-4x}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419916}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cc767f0c-f65c-5d40-bf26-8221c3e5652f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-\\frac{e^{-4x}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419916} :answer-field/id #uuid "fea0be10-7e7a-5e8c-b225-cbbbd6502e43" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419942}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "fb64e84b-4036-56ed-b5be-3b99c498406f" :question/math-academy-id "q-210762" :question/problem "Given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x)=2{e}^{-|4x|},\\,x\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),\n$$\n\nits cumulative distribution function is\n\n$$\nF(x)={\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{e}^{4x}}{2},\\, & x\\le 0 \\\\ h(x),\\, & x>0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $h(x)=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "Since our random variable $X$ has a probability distribution function $f(x)$ that involves an absolute value, the cumulative distribution function takes the following form:\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x)={\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{x}2{e}^{4t}\\,\\text{d}t, & x\\le 0 \\\\ {\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}2{e}^{4t}\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{0}^{x}2{e}^{-4t}\\,\\text{d}t, & x>0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's compute the integrals. \n\n- If $x\\le 0,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{x}2{e}^{4t}\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\frac{{e}^{4t}}{2}|}_{-\\infty }^{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{4x}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn particular, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}2{e}^{4t}\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\frac{{e}^{4x}}{2}|}_{x=0} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- If $x>0,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{x}2{e}^{-4t}\\,\\text{d}t & =-{\\frac{{e}^{-4t}}{2}|}_{0}^{x} \\\\  & =-\\frac{{e}^{-4x}}{2}+\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}2{e}^{4t}\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{0}^{x}2{e}^{-4t}\\,\\text{d}t & =\\frac{1}{2}+(-\\frac{{e}^{-4x}}{2}+\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =1-\\frac{{e}^{-4x}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the cumulative distribution function is given by\n\n$$\nF(x)={\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{e}^{4x}}{2},\\, & x\\le 0, \\\\ 1-\\frac{{e}^{-4x}}{2},\\, & x>0.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134159 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133727 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7b0ce833-e045-5aff-94a4-f9ad56cdb904" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a CDF Given a PDF That’s Nonzero Over All Real Numbers"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b8dd2c37-ec9c-5602-ab5a-e63c24ab6b8b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{e^{x}}{1+e^{x}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419908}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b8dd2c37-ec9c-5602-ab5a-e63c24ab6b8b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{e^{x}}{1+e^{x}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419908} :answer-field/id #uuid "13407dc0-5b13-5eaa-91b6-bca274b27437" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131063}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1bbb59a5-e080-5eb3-8f00-497d7dc7343f" :question/math-academy-id "q-210766" :question/problem "Given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{{e}^{x}}{(1+{e}^{x})^{2}},\\,x\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),\n$$\n\nfind the cumulative distribution function $F(x).$\n\n$F(x)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The cumulative distribution function of a continuous random variable $X$ is the function $F(x)$ defined by\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x)={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nFor the given probability density function, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(x) & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{x}\\frac{{e}^{t}}{(1+{e}^{t})^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={-\\frac{1}{1+{e}^{t}}|}_{-\\infty }^{x} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{1+{e}^{x}}+1 \\\\  & =1-\\frac{1}{1+{e}^{x}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{x}}{1+{e}^{x}}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186419943 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133728 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "eedcfa3d-b02b-5f96-99f4-cd0a452d272a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a CDF Given a PDF With Lower and Upper Bounds"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5b78d2ad-1275-5369-9916-4ad050ea2a49" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419877}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5b78d2ad-1275-5369-9916-4ad050ea2a49" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419877} :answer-field/id #uuid "37f12d01-f36a-528a-8df0-5d27379297ec" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419930}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "298016d0-4ea6-54d8-a832-231f3f8e4443" :question/math-academy-id "q-210784" :question/problem "Given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}1-\\frac{x}{2},\\, & 0\\le x\\le 2 \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nits cumulative distribution function is \n\n$$\nF(x)={\\begin{aligned}0,\\, & x<0 \\\\ h(x),\\, & 0\\le x\\le 2 \\\\ 1,\\, & x>2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $h(x)=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "Since our random variable $X$ has a probability distribution function $f(x)$ that is strictly positive only for $0\\le x\\le 2,$ the cumulative distribution function takes the following form:\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x)={\\begin{aligned}0, & x<0 \\\\ {\\int }_{0}^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t, & 0\\le x\\le 2 \\\\ 1, & x>2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the given probability density function, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{0}^{x}(1-\\frac{t}{2})\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ \\text{ } & ={(t-\\frac{{t}^{2}}{4})|}_{0}^{x} \\\\  & =x-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the cumulative distribution function is given by\n\n$$\nF(x)={\\begin{aligned}0, & x<0 \\\\ x-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}, & 0\\le x\\le 2 \\\\ 1, & x>2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186419954 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133728 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "eedcfa3d-b02b-5f96-99f4-cd0a452d272a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a CDF Given a PDF With Lower and Upper Bounds"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "92696a8b-4d36-591b-8359-09b0462c87c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^{4}-16}{240}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419899}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "92696a8b-4d36-591b-8359-09b0462c87c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^{4}-16}{240}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419899} :answer-field/id #uuid "b8a4a48c-0c9e-5eff-a6c5-6bb8647bf693" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419938}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d8d29abd-ea88-5ad4-8655-fbf6ab67a44c" :question/math-academy-id "q-210786" :question/problem "Given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{60}{x}^{3},\\, & 2\\le x\\le 4 \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nits cumulative distribution function is \n\n$$\nF(x)={\\begin{aligned}0,\\, & x<2 \\\\ h(x),\\, & 2\\le x\\le 4 \\\\ 1,\\, & x>4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $h(x)=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "Since our random variable $X$ has a probability distribution function $f(x)$ that is strictly positive only for $2\\le x\\le 4,$ the cumulative distribution function takes the following form:\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x)={\\begin{aligned}0, & x<2 \\\\ {\\int }_{2}^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t, & 2\\le x\\le 4 \\\\ 1, & x>4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the given probability density function, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{2}^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{2}^{x}\\frac{1}{60}{t}^{3}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ \\text{ } & ={\\frac{{t}^{4}}{240}|}_{2}^{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{4}}{240}-\\frac{1}{15}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the cumulative distribution function is given by\n\n$$\nF(x)={\\begin{aligned}0, & x<2 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{4}}{240}-\\frac{1}{15}, & 2\\le x\\le 4 \\\\ 1, & x>4.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186419955 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133728 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "eedcfa3d-b02b-5f96-99f4-cd0a452d272a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a CDF Given a PDF With Lower and Upper Bounds"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9092706e-4579-52cd-b336-558d7e1b9f64" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{3}}{324}+\\frac{{x}^{2}}{108}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419896}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9092706e-4579-52cd-b336-558d7e1b9f64" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{3}}{324}+\\frac{{x}^{2}}{108}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419896} :answer-field/id #uuid "fbd2268b-230b-5334-ac68-b3b22356482f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419941}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "dad3449e-8974-53d7-9ad6-1544954b39d1" :question/math-academy-id "q-210788" :question/problem "Given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{108}x(x+2),\\, & 0\\le x\\le 6 \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nits cumulative distribution function is \n\n$$\nF(x)={\\begin{aligned}0,\\, & x<0 \\\\ h(x),\\, & 0\\le x\\le 6 \\\\ 1,\\, & x>6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $h(x)=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "Since our random variable $X$ has a probability distribution function $f(x)$ that is strictly positive only for $0\\le x\\le 6,$ the cumulative distribution function takes the following form:\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x)={\\begin{aligned}0, & x<0 \\\\ {\\int }_{0}^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t, & 0\\le x\\le 6 \\\\ 1, & x>6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the given probability density function, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{0}^{x}\\frac{1}{108}t(t+2)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ \\text{ } & ={\\frac{1}{324}{t}^{2}(t+3)|}_{0}^{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{3}}{324}+\\frac{{x}^{2}}{108}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the cumulative distribution function is given by\n\n$$\nF(x)={\\begin{aligned}0, & x<0 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{3}}{324}+\\frac{{x}^{2}}{108}, & 0\\le x\\le 6 \\\\ 1, & x>6.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134538 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133726 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1d7509fa-a254-5b78-b307-3e0c4ef4d9ec" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a CDF Given a PDF With a Lower Bound"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fb6547f1-96a8-53cf-916f-dc7feeffac31" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186133269} {:answer/id #uuid "1d135339-50d4-589a-bbdd-9dfafdad32ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{1+x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419865} {:answer/id #uuid "7dac7e0d-2683-504c-998e-6a8f2452bc74" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419888} {:answer/id #uuid "86dc2cb8-34c2-59e1-b615-ac22c665e6f0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419891} {:answer/id #uuid "9212ec56-6681-5b9b-8850-605544afb5ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-\\frac{1}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419898}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9212ec56-6681-5b9b-8850-605544afb5ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-\\frac{1}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419898} :answer-field/id #uuid "cf38f8f6-64a3-5a95-aeb0-d81da3820d46" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186133266}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c465042c-a7c3-596c-abfd-e2cc0c1e779a" :question/math-academy-id "q-89137" :question/problem "Given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}},\\, & x\\ge 1 \\\\ 0,\\, & x<1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nits cumulative distribution function is \n\n$$\nF(x)={\\begin{aligned}0,\\, & x<1 \\\\ h(x),\\, & x\\ge 1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind the function $h(x).$" :question/worked-solution "Since our random variable $X$ has a probability distribution function $f(x)$ that is strictly positive only for $x\\ge 1,$ the cumulative distribution function takes the following form:\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x)={\\begin{aligned}0, & x<1 \\\\ {\\int }_{1}^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t, & x\\ge 1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the given probability density function, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{1}^{x}\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ \\text{ } & ={-\\frac{1}{t}|}_{1}^{x} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{x}+1 \\\\  & =1-\\frac{1}{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the cumulative distribution function is given by\n\n$$\nF(x)={\\begin{aligned}0, & x<1, \\\\ 1-\\frac{1}{x}, & x\\ge 1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186419953 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133726 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1d7509fa-a254-5b78-b307-3e0c4ef4d9ec" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a CDF Given a PDF With a Lower Bound"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4b6bc818-cf5d-5fbf-8f54-469f90018d9d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-\\frac{1}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419874} {:answer/id #uuid "9121cbd0-f9a1-5785-bcd2-b0cf0a5368c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419897} {:answer/id #uuid "ae3913fb-6c1f-5066-a107-fc615c4d98c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-\\frac{2}{x+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419906} {:answer/id #uuid "baa7e096-af04-58c0-9b33-2d21728b4311" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419910} {:answer/id #uuid "ce921dda-8563-59de-b3fe-a15f6ce57053" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1+\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419917}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9121cbd0-f9a1-5785-bcd2-b0cf0a5368c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419897} :answer-field/id #uuid "9e86a899-b91b-5d71-978f-830f6bac2bb2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419935}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d87af21c-48b4-5612-ae7a-18902b89c926" :question/math-academy-id "q-89546" :question/problem "Given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{{x}^{3}},\\, & x\\ge 1 \\\\ 0,\\, & x<1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nits cumulative distribution function is \n\n$$\nF(x)={\\begin{aligned}0,\\, & x<1 \\\\ h(x),\\, & x\\ge 1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind the function $h(x).$" :question/worked-solution "Since our random variable $X$ has a probability distribution function $f(x)$ that is strictly positive only for $x\\ge 1,$ the cumulative distribution function takes the following form:\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x)={\\begin{aligned}0, & x<1 \\\\ {\\int }_{1}^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t, & x\\ge 1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the given probability density function, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{1}^{x}\\frac{2}{{t}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ \\text{ } & ={-\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}}|}_{1}^{x} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}+1 \\\\  & =1-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the cumulative distribution function is given by\n\n$$\nF(x)={\\begin{aligned}0, & x<1, \\\\ 1-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}, & x\\ge 1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186419950 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133727 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7b0ce833-e045-5aff-94a4-f9ad56cdb904" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a CDF Given a PDF That’s Nonzero Over All Real Numbers"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4f0f787d-1687-5d7b-90fc-bcc440b2102f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "F(x)=\\frac{\\operatorname{arctan}⁡{e}^{x}-1}{\\pi }" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419875} {:answer/id #uuid "6178be04-2216-5153-b323-5257d0136d60" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "F(x)=\\frac{2\\operatorname{arctan}⁡{e}^{x}}{\\pi }" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419880} {:answer/id #uuid "9506108c-e704-538c-b7